  "question": {
    "text": "The molarity of a $70 \\%$ (mass $/$ mass) aqueous solution of a monobasic acid $(\\mathrm{X})$ is __________ $\\times 10^{-1}$ M(Nearest integer)\n[Given: Density of aqueous solution of (X) is $1.25 \\mathrm{~g} \\mathrm{~mL}^{-1}$\nMolar mass of the acid is $70 \\mathrm{~g} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$ ]",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "125",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Moles of solute $=\\frac{70}{70}=1$\nVolume of solution $=\\frac{100}{1.25}=80 \\mathrm{~mL}$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& M=\\frac{1}{80} \\times 1000=12.5 \\\\\n& M=125 \\times 10^{-1}\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
